From 84a2ed1526fd8115a123e7ce8797f347b6c4dcde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:40:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-91: F2 edits the control's text right on the
 design surface, like WPF (0.91.0)

WPF (XAML Designer keyboard shortcuts): "Edit control text | F2 (Esc to
exit)". Here F2 on the surface renamed the component (WPF renames in the
Properties window's Name box). Now F2 (ht9045Designer.editText) asks the probe
to open a text box over the selected control (its text, font, alignment; a
locked one or one without a text is refused and said): Enter or leaving it =
the same caption edit as the properties panel's (one Ctrl+Z), Esc = nothing.
While it is open the probe's first window key listener takes its keys (the
page may take Esc for itself -- found by the test: the HotPlate page did), its
clicks are not stopped (the caret), the clipboard is the box's own, and the
extension sets ht9045Designer.textEditing: every design-surface key rule is
off, Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y / Ctrl+Shift+Z go to the box (textUndo), never the page's
undo. Selecting something else, zooming or the operate mode ends it (kept).
Renaming stays in the Name box, F2 in the component tree and the right-click
menu (their texts say so).

WPF_DIFF_LOG.md: item 20 done (the 0.88 / 0.90 commits filled in); new open
items 21 (grid shown / snapping apart), 22 (baseline snaplines); the Toolbox
search box needs no change (a VS Code tree filters by typing).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 159, smoke 182, panels, real VS Code 157):
probe (F2 opens the box with Save2, arrows do not move, a press in it is not
stopped, Enter writes Save3, Esc writes nothing); smoke (F2 bound to editText,
the context set, no surface rule without the guard, Ctrl+Z to the box);
real VS Code (the box opens on spbSave, closed without writing, the source
untouched).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
